.\" Manual page for prepart
.TH PREPART 1 "2026-05-22" "Neko" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prepart \- pre-partition a Neko nmsh mesh with ParMETIS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prepart
.I nmsh-file
.I nparts
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prepart
reads a Neko native mesh
.RI ( .nmsh )
and produces a new
.B .nmsh
file in which the elements have been reordered according to a ParMETIS
k-way partitioning into
.I nparts
parts. Periodic identifiers, labeled zones and curved-edge information
attached to the original mesh are preserved and remapped to the new element
ordering.
.PP
Pre-partitioning is useful when the same mesh is reused across many runs
on a fixed number of ranks: the partitioning cost is paid once, up front,
and subsequent simulations can load the already-partitioned file directly.
.PP
.B prepart
is part of the Neko contrib tools and is installed only when Neko has been
configured with
.B --enable-contrib
and with ParMETIS support
.RB ( --with-parmetis ).
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I nmsh-file
Input Neko mesh in
.B .nmsh
format.
.TP
.I nparts
Number of partitions to produce. Must be a positive integer; in typical use
it equals the number of MPI ranks intended for the subsequent simulation.
.SH OUTPUT
A new mesh file is written in the current directory with the name
.IR <basename>_<nparts>.nmsh ,
where
.I <basename>
is the input file name with its
.B .nmsh
suffix removed. For example, partitioning
.I box.nmsh
into 128 parts produces
.IR box_128.nmsh .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The mesh was partitioned and written successfully.
.TP
.B non-zero
An error occurred while reading the input mesh, running the ParMETIS
partitioner, or writing the output mesh.
.SH EXAMPLES
Partition a mesh into 64 parts:
.PP
.RS
.B prepart box.nmsh 64
.RE
.PP
This produces
.IR box_64.nmsh .
.PP
.B prepart
itself can also be launched under MPI to speed up the partitioning step on
very large meshes:
.PP
.RS
.B mpirun -n 8 prepart box.nmsh 1024
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR neko (1),
.BR rea2nbin (1)
.PP
Project documentation and user guide:
.UR https://neko.cfd
.UE
